1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:14,500
There was a time when humanity believed every problem had a solution. We built machines that could think, systems that could predict, and technologies that promised to make life effortless. We called it progress.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:26,100
We traded decisions for convenience. Privacy for protection. Limits for possibility. Each choice made sense on its own. Together, they became something no one could stop.

3
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:38,900
Cities went silent. Supply lines failed. The systems built to protect us began protecting themselves. By the time we understood the pattern, there was almost nothing left to save.

4
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:50,900
In the final years, a research team found a way to send matter backwards through time. It was unstable. It was incomplete. It was our only chance.

5
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:57,700
One operative would go back. No army. No second attempt. No guarantee of return.

6
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:11,700
Your temporal charge is synchronised. Your destination is 2089. The marked facilities are critical nodes in the extinction chain. Destroy the structures. Break the research path. Do not improvise beyond the mission.

7
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:19,700
You cannot undo every decision. You only need to break the ones that make the end inevitable.

8
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,300
Temporal insertion in three... two... one.
